  The hit cells are the positive control: a matched detection is inside the
  radius by definition, so their act/centre ~0.85+ and 100% peak-in-R are what
  a working probe MUST show, not a finding.

  For the two MISS cells, 'floor peak in R' is the whole question:
   - peak inside R  -> the model DID localize the ramp and the detection was
     lost downstream, to the shipped threshold or to the greedy matcher handing
     the peak to an adjacent GT. Recoverable WITHOUT a second model.
   - peak outside R -> nothing of THIS ramp's to promote. 'act' there is usually
     a neighbouring peak's shoulder reaching into the window (nearest peak 1-2 R
     away, argmax on the window edge), not mass the extractor overlooked -- the
     profile below says which, per cell.

